infographic sequence-funnel-simple
data
  title Batching collapses syscalls per 1M ops
  desc Each step removes more user-kernel crossings — from one per op to near zero
  sequences
    - label 1,000,000 syscalls / 1M ops
      desc One write() per op — pure transition overhead, ~1-5µs each
    - label ~1,000 syscalls / 1M ops
      desc Buffer ~1k records, flush as one writev() or io_uring_enter()
    - label ~0 syscalls / 1M ops
      desc io_uring + SQPOLL: kernel polls the ring under sustained load
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #10b981
